<body lang="EN-ZA" link="blue" vlink="purple" style="word-wrap:break-word">
<div class="WordSection1">
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Hi Kevin,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<div style="mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm">
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Please remember to always include or Cc the API Support email address (<a href="mailto:api@accounting.sageone.co.za">api@accounting.sageone.co.za</a>) when you reply.
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Our personal e-mail addresses are not always monitored and could result in poor service should an email go unattended for any reason.
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">We work on a rotational basis, the above-mentioned email address is always monitored and your email would be attended to quicker.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="border:none;padding:0cm"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
</div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Kindly provide a detailed process flow as well as the daily frequency for each endpoint you have claimed.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Please note that we have noted your previous replies, however they do not provide a clear picture, and we cannot properly evaluate your solution and its impact on the API and overall performance
 of the system.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">Regards,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US">The Accounting API Team<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<div>
<div style="border:none;border-top:solid #E1E1E1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm">
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">From:</span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif"> KEVIN AMAYI &lt;kevinamayi20@gmail.com&gt;
<br>
<b>Sent:</b> Monday, 31 March 2025 14:02<br>
<b>To:</b> Kubushi, Joewie &lt;JoewieHarvey.Kubushi@sage.com&gt;<br>
<b>Subject:</b> Re: Still Following up on the Live API<o:p></o:p></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<table class="MsoNormalTable" border="1" cellspacing="3" cellpadding="0" width="100%" style="width:100.0%;background:#FFFFC0;border:none;border-left:solid black 2.25pt">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="border:none;padding:3.75pt 3.75pt 7.5pt 3.75pt">
<p class="MsoNormal"><acronym><b><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:black">EXTERNAL EMAIL</span></b></acronym><o:p></o:p></p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<div>
<div>
<p class="gmail-">Dear Joewie,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="gmail-">Thank you for your email and for outlining the API usage limits in Section 12 of the Developer Services License Agreement. We appreciate the clarity on these standards and are committed to ensuring full compliance with Sage’s API policies.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="gmail-">Based on the specified limitations, we have reviewed our request strategy and will make the following adjustments to remain within the allowed thresholds:<o:p></o:p></p>
<ul type="disc">
<li class="gmail-" style="mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Daily Request Limit (Section 12.4.2):</span></strong> Our system will ensure that the total number of API requests does not exceed 2,500 per day per company,
 even though enforcement of this limit is not currently in place.<o:p></o:p></li><li class="gmail-" style="mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Per-Minute Request Limit (Section 12.4.1):</span></strong> We will maintain a request frequency of no more than one request per second to avoid surpassing
 the limit of 100 requests per minute. This will also prevent any risk of receiving an HTTP 429 error and a temporary one-hour IP block.<o:p></o:p></li><li class="gmail-" style="mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Resource-Intensive API Calls (Section 12.4.5):</span></strong> We will minimize the use of API calls that have a high impact on system performance.<o:p></o:p></li><li class="gmail-" style="mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Fair Usage and System Performance Considerations (Sections 12.4.3 &amp; 12.4.4):</span></strong> We recognize that Sage Accounting is optimized for small business
 usage, and we will ensure that our API interactions remain within the reasonable operational limits of 3,000 customers, 3,000 suppliers, 5,000 items, 1,000 customer invoices, 1,000 supplier invoices, and 2,000 bank transactions per month to prevent any adverse
 effects on reporting and overall system performance.<o:p></o:p></li><li class="gmail-" style="mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Future Adjustments (Section 12.4.6):</span></strong> We will monitor any updates to Sage’s API limits and adjust our integration accordingly to maintain
 compliance with any revised thresholds or enforcement mechanisms.<o:p></o:p></li></ul>
<p class="gmail-">Please let us know if you have any additional recommendations or requirements that we should consider. We appreciate your guidance in ensuring seamless API integration.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="gmail-">That said, we kindly request that this issue be resolved as urgently as possible to avoid disruptions that could slow down operations and frustrate our processes. A swift resolution would be highly appreciated to maintain a smooth experience
 for all stakeholders.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="gmail-">Looking forward to your prompt response.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="gmail-">Best regards,<br>
<strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Kevin Amayi Musungu.</span></strong><br>
<strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Chief Technology Officer (CTO)</span></strong><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<div>
<div>
<p class="MsoNormal">On Mon, Mar 31, 2025 at 2:21<span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> </span>PM Kubushi, Joewie &lt;<a href="mailto:JoewieHarvey.Kubushi@sage.com">JoewieHarvey.Kubushi@sage.com</a>&gt; wrote:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<blockquote style="border:none;border-left:solid #CCCCCC 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm">
<div>
<div>
<div>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">Hi David,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">Kindly note that the frequency you have provided adheres to the daily limit but does not comply with the other limitations.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">I have copied the usage limits of our API from Section 12 of our Developer Services License Agreement below for your reference:<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">12.4. Usage limits for the API:<br>
<br>
12.4.1. A limit of 100 requests can be made per minute per company. If this request limit is exceeded, the API will return HTTP 429 (Request Limit Reached) with the message “Your IP address has exceeded the allowed number of transactions per minute and has
 been blocked for 1 hour”. Your IP address will be blocked for 1 hour. It is advisable to make no more than one request per second to avoid this.<br>
<br>
12.4.2. A limit of 2,500 requests can be made per day per company. Although these limits are not currently enforced, please consider this limit when calling the API. These limits will be enforced in future.<span style="color:red"><br>
</span><br>
<span style="color:red">12.4.3. Sage Accounting is an accounting application for small businesses, with intended usage around 3,000 customers, 3,000 suppliers, 5,000 items and 1,000 customer invoices, 1,000 supplier invoices and 2,000 bank transactions per
 month. Users will experience performance issues, in particular with reporting, with companies that exceed reasonable usage.</span><br>
<br>
12.4.4. The API and all users using the API are limited to a finite pool of resources. Should these resources be exceeded, in order to maintain the performance and stability of the Sage Accounting accounting application, resource governing will take place.
 This will affect all API users and all users are encouraged to adhere to the fair usage policies and rate limits.<br>
<br>
12.4.5. While all API calls are limited per minute and per day, some API calls are a lot heavier than others and will have a significant impact on the Sage Accounting service as a whole, if used too frequently. The API calls listed in this section are to be
 kept to a minimum – as excessive use of these calls will mean performance degradation. If excessive use of these calls is detected, API keys will be blocked without warning. This list includes, but is not limited to Detailed Ledger Transaction, Customer Ageing
 and Supplier Ageing, Customer Statement and Supplier Statement, Account Balance, Cash Movement, Item Movement, Outstanding Customer and Supplier Documents, all Transaction Listings, Allocations, Budget, Take On Balance, Trial Balance, Tax Reports.<br>
<br>
12.4.6. Sage Accounting may revisit the “per minute” and “per day” limits in the future.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">Please provide a revised frequency that ensures all stipulated API limits(not limited to those highlighted in red) are adhered to, and will not affect the overall performance of
 SBCA.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">Regards,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">The Accounting API Team<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<div>
<div style="border:none;border-top:solid #E1E1E1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm">
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">From:</span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif"> Prof
 David Amukowa &lt;<a href="mailto:davyamukowa@gmail.com" target="_blank">davyamukowa@gmail.com</a>&gt;
<br>
<b>Sent:</b> Monday, 31 March 2025 13:12<br>
