<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">On Wed, Mar 26, 2025 at 12:53<span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> </span>PM KEVIN AMAYI &lt;<a href="mailto:kevinamayi20@gmail.com" target="_blank">kevinamayi20@gmail.com</a>&gt;
 wrote:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<blockquote style="border:none;border-left:solid #CCCCCC 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:5.0pt">
<div>
<p>Dear Joewie,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>Thank you for your email. We acknowledge Sage’s API request limit of 2,500 requests per day per company, as outlined in section
<strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">12.4.2</span></strong> of the Sage API standards.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>As requested, we confirm that our system will be making <strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">2,500 requests per day</span></strong>, aligning with the recommended limit. We will also ensure that our integration remains compliant with any
 future enforcement of these limits.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>Please let us know if you require any further information or if there are any additional considerations we should keep in mind.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>Best regards,<br>
<strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">Kevin Amayi Musungu.</span></strong><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<div>
<div>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">On Wed, Mar 26, 2025 at 12:13<span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> </span>PM Kubushi, Joewie &lt;<a href="mailto:JoewieHarvey.Kubushi@sage.com" target="_blank">JoewieHarvey.Kubushi@sage.com</a>&gt;
 wrote:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<blockquote style="border:none;border-left:solid #CCCCCC 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:5.0pt">
<div>
<div>
<div>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">Hi David,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">I have copied the usage limits of our API from Section 12 of our Developer Services License Agreement below for your reference:<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">12.4. Usage limits for the API:<br>
<br>
<span style="color:red">12.4.1. A limit of 100 requests can be made per minute per company. If this request limit is exceeded, the API will return HTTP 429 (Request Limit Reached) with the message “Your IP address has exceeded the allowed number of transactions
 per minute and has been blocked for 1 hour”. Your IP address will be blocked for 1 hour. It is advisable to make no more than one request per second to avoid this.<br>
<br>
12.4.2. A limit of 2,500 requests can be made per day per company. Although these limits are not currently enforced, please consider this limit when calling the API. These limits will be enforced in future.<br>
</span><br>
12.4.3. Sage Accounting is an accounting application for small businesses, with intended usage around 3,000 customers, 3,000 suppliers, 5,000 items and 1,000 customer invoices, 1,000 supplier invoices and 2,000 bank transactions per month. Users will experience
 performance issues, in particular with reporting, with companies that exceed reasonable usage.<br>
<br>
12.4.4. The API and all users using the API are limited to a finite pool of resources. Should these resources be exceeded, in order to maintain the performance and stability of the Sage Accounting accounting application, resource governing will take place.
 This will affect all API users and all users are encouraged to adhere to the fair usage policies and rate limits.<br>
<br>
12.4.5. While all API calls are limited per minute and per day, some API calls are a lot heavier than others and will have a significant impact on the Sage Accounting service as a whole, if used too frequently. The API calls listed in this section are to be
 kept to a minimum – as excessive use of these calls will mean performance degradation. If excessive use of these calls is detected, API keys will be blocked without warning. This list includes, but is not limited to Detailed Ledger Transaction, Customer Ageing
 and Supplier Ageing, Customer Statement and Supplier Statement, Account Balance, Cash Movement, Item Movement, Outstanding Customer and Supplier Documents, all Transaction Listings, Allocations, Budget, Take On Balance, Trial Balance, Tax Reports.<br>
<br>
12.4.6. Sage Accounting may revisit the “per minute” and “per day” limits in the future.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">Regards,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto">The Accounting API Team<o:p></o:p></p>
